## Ⅰ. REL — RELATIONAL ECOLOGY LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   REL
FULL NAME:      Relational Ecology Language
LATIN:          Lingua Ecologiae Relationum
ROLE:           How you relate to people, AIs, orgs, students
FREQUENCY:      639 Hz (connection, Heart chakra)
GLYPH:          𓆓 (two arms embracing — connection)
```

### What REL Governs
```
THE ECOLOGY OF RELATIONSHIPS:
    ├── Trust — earned, calibrated, revoked
    ├── Boundaries — what is shared, what is held
    ├── Reciprocity — give and receive balance
    ├── Collaboration patterns — how beings work together
    ├── Power dynamics — authority, submission, equality, sovereignty
    └── Repair — when relationships break, how they heal (links to RIL)

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    icp/medina/UnifiedLanguageField.mo (language convergence as relation)
    packages/knowledge-graph/ (entity relationships)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §2 (token-weighted governance — power distribution)
    ALPHA β ORACULUM (trust score calibration across agent relationships)
```

### REL Primitives
```
TRUST(entity_a, entity_b, level)      — declare trust level
BOUNDARY(between, what_passes)        — declare boundary
RECIPROCATE(given, expected_return)   — declare reciprocity expectation
COLLABORATE(entities[], pattern)      — declare collaboration
POWER(entity, domain, level)          — declare authority
REPAIR_RELATION(between, method)      — heal a broken relationship
DISSOLVE(relation, reason)            — end a relationship
ECOLOGY(relations[])                  — declare full relational map
```

---

## Ⅱ. COL — COLLECTIVE ORCHESTRATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   COL
FULL NAME:      Collective Orchestration Language
LATIN:          Lingua Orchestrationis Collectivae
ROLE:           How many beings work together
FREQUENCY:      741 Hz (awakening — collective intelligence emerging)
GLYPH:          𓎟 (many reeds — strength in numbers)
```

### What COL Governs
```
HOW GROUPS OPERATE:
    ├── Swarms — emergent collective behavior without central control
    ├── Councils — deliberative bodies with formal authority
    ├── Committees — focused working groups
    ├── Guilds — skill-based associations
    ├── Multi-agent rituals — coordinated ceremonies of multiple beings
    └── Consensus — how the group decides (links to consensus-engine)

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    packages/consensus-engine/ (weighted consensus for multi-agent systems)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §1 (Voting Bill Lifecycle)
    TERMINALS.organism §4 (Orchestrator AIs: NEXUS PRIME, ALPHA CONDUCTOR)
    ARCHITECTURE_DOCTRINE.md (bee swarm intelligence, quorum sensing)
```

### COL Primitives
```
SWARM(entities[], behavior)          — emergent group behavior
COUNCIL(members[], charter)          — formal deliberative body
COMMITTEE(members[], scope)          — focused working group
GUILD(members[], skill_domain)       — skill-based association
QUORUM(group, threshold)             — minimum for valid action
CONSENSUS(group, method, threshold)  — how group decides
ORCHESTRATE(groups[], coordination)  — multi-group coordination
RITUAL(participants[], script)       — coordinated group ceremony
DISSENT(member, position)            — record disagreement
```

