## Ⅲ. ROL — ROLE LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   ROL
FULL NAME:      Role Language
LATIN:          Lingua Munerum
ROLE:           How roles are defined, swapped, merged
FREQUENCY:      417 Hz (transmutation — roles shift and transform)
GLYPH:          𓊃 (throne seat — the seat changes, the person changes)
```

### What ROL Governs
```
ROLE MECHANICS:
    ├── Definition — what a role IS (capabilities, duties, authority)
    ├── Assignment — how roles are given to beings
    ├── Swapping — how beings change roles
    ├── Merging — how multiple roles combine in one being
    ├── Hierarchy — how roles relate in authority chains
    └── Temporal roles — "today a critic, tomorrow a builder"

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    packages/role-engine/ (RBAC + ABAC hybrid)
    TERMINALS.organism §4 (6 AGIs, 2 Alpha AGIs, 3 Engine AIs, 3 Solver AIs, 4 Orchestrators)
    packages/consensus-engine/ (DEFAULT_ROLE_WEIGHTS: SOVEREIGN=1.00 → RESEARCHER=0.50)
    GOVERNANCE.organism (role-engine authority assignments)
```

### ROL Primitives
```
ROLE(id, capabilities[], duties[], authority)  — define role
ASSIGN(being, role, duration)                  — assign role to being
SWAP(being, from_role, to_role)                — change roles
MERGE(being, roles[])                          — combine roles
HIERARCHY(roles[], order)                      — define authority order
WEIGHT(role, domain, weight)                   — set role weight
TEMPORAL(being, role, schedule)                — time-bound role
REVOKE(being, role, reason)                    — remove role
DELEGATE(from_being, to_being, authority)      — delegate authority
```

